{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Eliab: Nemuel, and Dathan, and Abiram — those are Dathan and Abiram</b>. Scripture mentions this to make known that the entire inheritance from the family of the Palluit remained to Nemuel alone, for Dathan and Abiram and all that was theirs were swallowed up. Or, according to the words of our Sages (Bava Batra 118a), to hint that they lost their portion in the land even though they were among those who came out of Egypt and were fit for an inheritance."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:42.448125770Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}